    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_ff10988b73232ae17e7eb2749d2af47748bb4a5d16b0add22b18564106912fd6",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "RH is recoded into square-root-scale control of two complementary summatory observables. The von Mangoldt sum measures deviation of prime-power weight from its main term through several equivalent error bounds, including an explicit finite-range inequality; the Möbius sum measures cancellation of squarefree signs through two equivalent growth bounds. The shared RH equivalence does not make the observables identical or prove any of the bounds.",
