      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a9163ff27fe353b36e9c3c1a3247f16f99144ca5dba1d802e1046bc0eaf76975",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Three alternative encodings replace direct zero location by different parameter structures: the de Bruijn-Newman family asks on which side of a real-rootedness threshold the undeformed Xi lies, Grommer's construction asks for positive determinants at every coefficient-matrix size, and Redheffer's divisibility matrices ask for an asymptotic determinant-growth bound as n increases.",
