    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a916e22a824f98783f673660b8a56118e24dcb1f2f9360eefb3e1a9055ff4b81",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the source's L-function examples, gamma and conductor factors complete Dirichlet-series functions into objects reflected about s=1/2; recentering s=1/2+iz turns that reflection into z-to-minus-z symmetry, while Hardy's phase normalization makes critical-line values real. The same geometry then defines RH-type assertions over different L-function families, and critical-line zeros become real zeros in the centered variable.",
